                           </imprint>
                           <title level="a" xml:id="title_2d74cddb">De tvende Borgerdydskolers 100 Aars Jubilæum</title>
                           <title level="j" xml:id="title_8efde905">Nationaltidende</title>
                           <biblScope unit="issue" xml:id="biblScope_899220a4">Tillæg til Nr. 3950</biblScope>
                           <biblScope unit="page" xml:id="biblScope_b6b6896f">1</biblScope>
                        </bibl>
                     </biblList>
                  </event>
               </eventList>
               <p xml:id="idm167">In 1787 Selskabet for Borgerdyd (The Society for Civic Virtue) founded a private school for boys, which the following year was divided into two. In 1813-1843 the school in the inner Copenhagen was housed in the building of the publishing firm Gyldendal in Klareboderne, later in Bredgade and from 1884 in Stockholmsgade, whereas the other school in 1795 moved to Strandgade on Christianshavn. Hartmann had been a pupil at the school in Klareboderne in the second half of the 1810s.</p>
            </history>
